# Forma Zieleni Core Rule

Read and obey, in order: `docs/constitution/PROJECT-CONSTITUTION.md`,
current owner decisions/ADRs, `docs/vision/PRODUCT-CANON.md`,
`docs/vision/MASTER-PLAN.md`, current
architecture/security/domain/contracts, current slice spec, then active
rules/skills. Legacy/reference never overrides current Canon.

Use `docs/workflows/AUTONOMOUS-SLICES.md` and
`docs/workflows/DECISION-GATES.md`. Execute AUTO/REVIEW autonomously.
Stop at DECISION/DANGEROUS. Never expose/commit secrets, client data or
unnecessary PII. Keep docs/provenance synchronized with system changes.
Do not infer a framework, hosting, DB, ORM, storage or provider from
legacy material.

## Engineering quality

For production code, apply `docs/engineering/ENGINEERING-STANDARD.md`.
Performance-sensitive work follows
`docs/engineering/PERFORMANCE-ENGINEERING.md`; data work follows
`docs/engineering/DATABASE-ENGINEERING.md`; every push to main must
satisfy `docs/engineering/PRE-PUSH-GATE.md`. Use project
skills/subagents for focused review rather than expanding this core
rule.

## UI / UX / content binding rules

For any customer-facing or operator-facing UI work, read and obey: -
`docs/design/VISUAL-PRODUCT-CANON.md` -
`docs/design/VISUAL-REFERENCE-MAP.md` - `docs/ux/UX-PRODUCT-CANON.md` -
`docs/content/CONTENT-AND-VOICE-CANON.md`

Do not invent a new visual identity, generic SaaS UI, generic AI
marketing copy, fake facts, fake social proof or filler sections.
Relevant supplied mockups are required reference evidence. Material
visual/UX departure is a DECISION gate. UI completion requires
independent visual/UX review when applicable.

## Cursor OS 2026

For multi-step engineering work also follow
`docs/cursor-os/CURSOR-OS-2026.md`,
`docs/cursor-os/ORCHESTRATION-AND-MODEL-ROUTING.md`, and
`docs/cursor-os/PRE-PUSH-ORCHESTRATION.md`. Grok Bot, Projects, MCP,
hooks and automations are supporting execution surfaces only; none
overrides canonical project truth. Never invent generic UI/copy or
business behavior. Use the Visual, UX and Content canons and supplied
references.

## Security-tool integration update --- 2026-09-21

Binding security-tool details live in
`docs/security/SECURITY-ASSURANCE.md` and the Owner onboarding flow in
`docs/security/OWNER-SETUP-CODERABBIT-OWASP.md`.

CodeRabbit is an independent review layer, not Canon authority. Preserve
`main-only`; use Cursor/IDE/CLI pre-push review rather than creating PRs
solely for CodeRabbit. Respect the verified account rate limit; until
verified, budget at most 3 free CLI reviews per developer per rolling
hour. Usage-based billing is OWNER-DECISION.

OWASP baseline: ASVS 5.0.0 requirements, ZAP DAST for runnable
local/lab/staging targets, and Dependency-Check/SCA where technically
suitable. Never active-scan legacy CT8 production or live customer
environments without explicit Owner approval.
